# Scraper output — large, machine-specific, and stale by the time anyone
# reads it. Sample files are the one deliberate exception (CLAUDE.md §2).
*.json
*.csv
!sample_output.json
!sample_output.csv
zimmo_listings.*
*_debug.html
*_debug.png

# Local diagnostics / live-test working directory — and ANY run directory by
# kind, not one chosen name (a sibling committed a raw dump through `live/`),
# plus paged dumps like X.page3 (family template §24, §26).
live_results/
live/
out/
output/
runs/
results/
tmp/
scratch/
dumps/
captures/
*.page[0-9]*

# Ad-hoc, one-off diagnostic/analysis scripts written DURING a live-
# testing session (confirmed real gap: none of these were excluded
# automatically, and all had to be removed by hand before this repo's
# own first commit). Going forward, name any new one-off script
# starting with `scratch_` so this pattern catches it automatically;
# these specific names are also listed directly since they already
# exist in this project's own history and might be recreated verbatim.
scratch_*
*_scratch.py
reliability_test.sh
reliability_run_*
reliability_logs/
check_context.py
check_quality.py
check_dup.py
extract_jsonld.py
analyze_reliability.py

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.fingerprint_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Secrets and logs — NEVER commit these
*.log
*.key
secrets*

# Every spelling of a working .env, not just `.env`: a `.env.bak` or
# `.env.local` is exactly how a live key gets one `git add -A` from a commit
# (family template §22). The negation keeps the documented example tracked.
.env*
!.env.example
